## § CORE-THESIS
v3's cost center ≠ its grammar (grammar = already near-optimal: telegraphic drop-order ✓, sigil-prefix ✓, think-blocks ✓).
cost center = RARE-UNICODE SURFACE: 3-byte BMP glyphs (-> <= 3 BPE tok each) vs ASCII digraphs (1-2).
∴ v4 = KEEP v3 semantics + slot-grammar ; REFACTOR surface to measured-cheapest form ; ADD line-IDs, terminator, budget-law.
+ no-galactic-notation'r: optimize MEASURED tok/proposition @ realistic trace-length on TARGET tokenizer ; ¬ bits/glyph theory.

## § V4-DELTA (from v3, decision-level)
D1 SURFACE: ASCII-default. alias-map (freeze post-S0 measurement):
   -> => ~> |> :: keep-as-is ✓(1-2tok) · § « » ¬ keep ✓(latin-1, 1-2tok)
   retire-to-alias: ⊗->(x) · ⟨⟩-><> · ⌈⌉->[! !] · ⟦⟧->[[ ]] · ⟪⟫->T[ ] · «»-optional
   evidence-marks: ✓◐○✗⊘△▽‼ -> y ~ p x ? h dep !!   (1 tok each, measured-pending S0)
   modals unchanged (already ASCII): W! R! M? N! I> Q? P> D>
D2 LINE-GRAMMAR'r: 1 proposition/line · sigil-first · fixed slots (subj rel obj gate) · RPN-order where it deletes brackets
D3 LINE-IDs + BACKREF: `L7:` labels ; refer `@L7` ¬ restate (delta-encoding ; cable-code principle)
D4 TERMINATOR: `!ans` closes every think-block (TALE elasticity: unclosed budget -> verbosity-compensation)
D5 VALUE-TOKEN LAW ‼: numbers, intermediate results, bindings = NEVER compressed (CoT-tokens-as-variables, arXiv:2505.04955) ;
   compress coherence only ; hardest step gets MOST tokens (inverse-naive)
D6 BUDGET: easy-step draft <=5 tok (CoD) · load-bearing step = unbudgeted · per-block soft-cap declared at open `B:40`
D7 LEGEND: 1-line resident catalog @context-top + expand-on-novel-construct (ICL-grounding: brittle w/o examples)
D8 CODEBOOK: recurring multi-token concept -> assigned short ID @first-use (`K1=sheaf-coboundary-energy`) ; Toki-Pona
   verbosity-paradox'r: N! over-minimize inventory
D9 PLACEMENT: problem+constraints @top · frontier @bottom (lost-in-middle U-curve) — v3 think-block already complies ✓
D10 think-block sigils go ASCII: P: D: T: S: C: (v3 §P.. stays valid input)

## § APOCRYPHA-COUPLING (3 rings ; regime-tagged per galactic-lens)
R0 AGENT-CoT [PRACTICAL-NOW]: all workspace agent reasoning/handoffs/commit-msgs adopt v4 on ratification ;
   zero code change ; direct token-cost cut on every session.
R1 SPEC-SURFACE [PRACTICAL-NOW, post-ratify]: new specs written v4 ; existing v3 corpus stays valid (v4 reads v3) ;
   mechanical re-surface only-if-touched ; N! bulk-rewrite (churn ≻ value).
R2 SUBSTRATE [STRASSEN-CLASS, parked ⊗ trigger]: Apocrypha internals that PARSE CSL — wire/csl_frame.py ·
   src/cssl/ interpreter (spec-16) · lang/preamble — migrating these = code+tests+invariant surface.
   trigger'g = {v4 ratified ∧ G-V4-1 pass ∧ csl_frame parser-cost measured ∧ spec-16 owner-session}.
   until-trigger: substrate speaks v3, agents speak v4, both valid (dual-key period).
compounding-note: L1 memory tier stores raw traces -> denser notation compounds through every pyramid level
   (cheaper storage + more context/window + cheaper consolidation prompts). = POLICY≻SCALE family member.

